  - emberhex
  - tidelash
  - stormbolt
  - wildmend
  - greyward
  - stormcrownWrath
  creatures:
  - id: mistling
    name: Mistling
    body: shade
    color: '#8aa89a'
    weakness: Fire
    lore: A scrap of a forgotten soul, woven from fog. Drifts toward the living warmth it can no longer remember having.
    hp: 30
    speed: 46
    damage: 6
    attackRange: 18
    attackRate: 1.3
    aggroRange: 150
    size: 12
    xp: 12
    float: 1
    ranged: 0
    boss: 0
  - id: hollowHound
    name: Hollow Hound
    body: beast
    color: '#2a1f2e'
    weakness: Fire
    lore: A black hound of the Underway, hollow where its heart should be. It hunts the moment your torch gutters low.
    hp: 70
    speed: 88
    damage: 14
    attackRange: 20
    attackRate: 0.9
    aggroRange: 180
    size: 14
    xp: 26
    float: 0
    ranged: 0
    boss: 0
  - id: gorgythe
    name: Gorgythe
    body: serpent
    color: '#3f6d4a'
    weakness: Lightning
    lore: "A serpent-maned thing of the ruins. Do not meet the green light of its eyes for long \u2014 stone has a way of creeping in."
    hp: 90
    speed: 60
    damage: 16
    attackRange: 22
    attackRate: 1.1
    aggroRange: 160
    size: 15
    xp: 34
    float: 0
    ranged: 0
    boss: 0
  - id: strix
    name: Strix
    body: bird
    color: '#4a3a5a'
    weakness: Lightning
    lore: A night-bird out of the old curses, screaming omens. It flings feathers of shadow from above.
    hp: 60
    speed: 70
    damage: 14
    attackRange: 130
    attackRate: 1.5
    aggroRange: 200
    size: 13
    xp: 30
    float: 1
    ranged: 1
    boss: 0
  - id: bronzeWatcher
    name: Bronze Watcher
    body: automaton
    color: '#9a7a3a'
    weakness: Water
    lore: A guardian forged by Pyrrhon and bound to its post for an age. The sea's salt is its only undoing.
    hp: 150
    speed: 38
    damage: 24
    attackRange: 26
    attackRate: 1.8
    aggroRange: 150
    size: 18
    xp: 48
    float: 0
    ranged: 0
    boss: 0
  - id: cinderMaw
    name: Pyraketh, the Cinder-Maw
    body: beast
    color: '#6a2a1f'
    weakness: Water
    lore: A lion-bodied horror with a furnace for a throat, loosed from the deep caves. The Mistwood will not be free of fire until it falls.
    hp: 340
    speed: 40
    damage: 30
    attackRange: 30
    attackRate: 1.6
    aggroRange: 200
    size: 26
    xp: 150
    float: 0
    ranged: 1
    boss: 1
  quests:
  - id: awakening
    title: The Unmarked
    giver: oracle
    region: mistwood
    summary: The last Oracle, Theira, will teach you to channel a god's power.
    lore: The Veil has thinned around you for a reason. Learn to wield the fire in your blood, and the hidden world will open.
    next: stolenRelic
    objectives:
    - type: cast
      creature: 
      spell: emberhex
      item: 
      npc: 
      loc: 
      text: Cast Emberhex (press 1)
      count: 1
    - type: kill
      creature: mistling
      spell: 
      item: 
      npc: 
      loc: 
      text: Banish 3 Mistlings
      count: 3
    rewards:
      xp: 40
      gold: 20
      spell: 
      items:
      - nectarVial
  - id: stolenRelic
    title: The Stolen Relic
    giver: kassander
    region: mistwood
    summary: "The hero Kassander's heirloom \u2014 shards of a godless blade \u2014 were scattered by the shades. Recover them."
    lore: A demigod without their relic is half a hero. Kassander paces the wood, hunting the shades that robbed him.
    next: 
    objectives:
    - type: collect
      creature: 
      spell: 
      item: relicShard
      npc: 
      loc: 
      text: Recover 4 relic shards
      count: 4
    - type: talk
      creature: 
      spell: 
      item: 
      npc: kassander
      loc: 
      text: Return the shards to Kassander
      count: 0
    rewards:
      xp: 80
      gold: 50
      spell: stormbolt
      items: []
  - id: asphodel
    title: Flowers for the Dead
    giver: myrrha
    region: mistwood
    summary: Sister Myrrha needs sacred Asphodel blooms to keep the wood's restless dead at peace.
    lore: "The asphodel grows only where the dead lie thick. Its pale glow keeps the shades from waking \u2014 but the flowers are fading, and the dead stir."
    next: 
    objectives:
    - type: collect
      creature: 
      spell: 
      item: asphodel
      npc: 
      loc: 
      text: Gather 6 Asphodel blooms
      count: 6
    - type: talk
      creature: 
      spell: 
      item: 
      npc: myrrha
      loc: 
      text: Bring the blooms to Sister Myrrha
      count: 0
    rewards:
      xp: 90
      gold: 40
      spell: wildmend
      items:
      - TopChuk
  - id: trialBronze
    title: Trial of Bronze
    giver: kassander
    region: mistwood
    summary: Prove your worth against Pyrrhon's bound guardians to earn passage toward the drowned temple.
    lore: No demigod passes deeper into the hidden world without besting the bronze watchers. They do not tire. You must.
    next: 
    objectives:
    - type: kill
      creature: bronzeWatcher
      spell: 
      item: 
      npc: 
      loc: 
      text: Destroy 2 Bronze Watchers
      count: 2
    rewards:
      xp: 160
      gold: 80
      spell: 
      items:
      - ambrosiaCake
      - ambrosiaCake
  - id: cinderMaw
    title: The Cinder-Maw
    giver: oracle
    region: mistwood
    summary: A fire-throated horror has crawled up from the caves. End it before it burns the wood to ash.
    lore: The prophecy spoke of waking what sleeps. Something has woken early, and it is hungry. This is the first true test of the Unmarked.
    next: 
    objectives:
    - type: kill
      creature: cinderMaw
      spell: 
      item: 
      npc: 
      loc: 
      text: Slay Pyraketh, the Cinder-Maw
      count: 1
    - type: talk
      creature: 
      spell: 
      item: 
      npc: oracle
      loc: 
      text: Tell Theira the beast is slain
      count: 0
    rewards:
      xp: 240
      gold: 120
      spell: greyward
      items:
      - cinderSigil
  questOrder:
  - awakening
  - stolenRelic
  - asphodel
  - trialBronze
  - cinderMaw
  npcs:
  - id: oracle
    name: Theira, the Last Oracle
    region: mistwood
    color: '#caa8e8'
    role: Oracle of Aurelith
    greeting: So. The Veil spat you out at last. I have waited a long time for you, Unmarked one.
    tx: 18
    ty: 26
    lines:
    - "You crossed from the mortal world without knowing it \u2014 most never do. The glow in your blood is divine. You are a demigod, child of a god who has not yet claimed you."
    - "Press 1 to loose an Emberhex \u2014 Pyrrhon's gift, the first power most demigods find. Try it on those mistlings before they drink your warmth."
  - id: kassander
    name: Kassander the Unclaimed
    region: mistwood
    color: '#c89a5a'
    role: Demigod
    greeting: Another Unmarked. Good. The wood eats the ones who walk it alone.
    tx: 8
    ty: 18
    lines:
    - I have hunted monsters in this hidden world for thirty years and still no god has claimed me. Do not let that frighten you. A blade does not need a name to cut.
    - "The shades shattered my heirloom \u2014 a godless blade, forged before the Theurgoi. Bring me its shards and I will teach you the Stormcrown's lightning."
  - id: myrrha
    name: Sister Myrrha
    region: mistwood
    color: '#88c0a0'
    role: Priestess of Koravel
    greeting: Walk softly here. The dead sleep light beneath this moss.
    tx: 26
    ty: 16
    lines:
    - I tend the asphodel for Koravel, that the wood's dead may rest. While the pale flowers glow, the shades stay still.
    - "But the blooms are withering and the dead grow restless. Gather fresh asphodel \u2014 it glows among the graves \u2014 and the Green Crown will teach you her mending."
  - id: ferryman
    name: The Veiled Ferryman
    region: mistwood
    color: '#7a7a8a'
    role: ???
    greeting: You burn brighter than the others, Unmarked. The Veiled Queen has noticed.
    tx: 22
    ty: 36
    lines:
    - 'Six realms lie beyond this wood: a drowned temple, a city of shades, the caves that go down to Nyxara, a citadel of cold light, and the Threshold of the gods themselves.'
    - The prophecy walks with you whether you will it or not. Grow strong here first. The hidden world does not forgive the unready.
